SRC/dm -- changes made for the OSK freeware collection  Rebuilt 2026-09-26 from this source, -qm (trap-free), for an ANSI or  vt100 terminal.  The archive's binary needed cio.  Everything below is  #ifndef MM1 or leaves the MM1 branch as it was, so building with -dMM1  gives the MM/1 program back.  diskmaster.c: main() set stdout unbuffered.  This C library's printf()  writes control bytes in place of its text to an unbuffered stdout  (measured with a ten-line probe: each printf came out as a run of  bytes 1, 2, 3 and 5, while fputs and putc were correct), and that is what the first  -qm build of dm drew -- it looked like box characters losing bit 7 and  broken cursor codes, but the putc'd box bytes were intact and the  printf'd escape sequences were not there at all.  stdout stays buffered  now; diskmaster.h empties it before each wait (the keyboard poll,  sleep(), system()), and getchar() empties it by itself.  The MM1 build  still sets it unbuffered.  diskmaster.c: arrowkey().  An ANSI arrow key is ESC [ A or ESC O A; dm  read the ESC and flush_kbd() threw the rest away.  Up and down are now  read as the Ctrl-P and Ctrl-N the MM/1 keyboard sends, and Ctrl-P and  Ctrl-N still work.  screen.c: hilite() and plain().  The bar was drawn in colours alone,  which a vt100 cannot show.  Its colours are now sent swapped and then  reversed -- ESC [ 0;3b;4f;7m -- so a colour terminal shows the same  colours as before and a monochrome one shows reverse video.  showfiles.c  calls them where the bar is drawn.  The originals are diskmaster.c.ori, diskmaster.h.ori, screen.c.ori and  showfiles.c.ori.  The SECAD alib.l functions it calls come from the  driver's os9alib.c shim.  misc.c: the file-information pane printed RBF's year byte, years  since 1900, with %02d, so 2026 read `126'.  It prints the year modulo  100, as the program did when it was written.  The original is  misc.c.ori.  2026-09-26.  diskmaster.c: the space bar and the up arrow.  Space shows the last  20 entries, starting wherever that falls, and in a directory of fewer  than 20 it started before the first.  Up from the top of a window  then stepped back a whole 20, which from such a start went below the  first entry, and dm read names from before its own list; os9exec  stops it there with E_PRCABT.  Both now stop at the first entry.  misc.c: the file-information pane freed a pointer into the middle of  its own buffer, having moved it past `Length:' to print the rest.  It now prints through a second pointer and frees the one malloc()  gave it.  2026-10-01.